(Occupational Health Guidance for Outdoor Workers) Tj T*

(Document ID: REF-WRK-2024) Tj T*
(Source: Occupational Safety & Environmental Health Administration) Tj T*
(Topic: Construction, Delivery, Municipal, and Agricultural Worker Safety) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Occupational Protection Mandates:) Tj T*
(1. Employer Responsibilities: Monitor ambient air quality at job sites hourly when AQI exceeds 100.) Tj T*
(2. Respiratory Protection: Provide NIOSH-approved N95 or KN95 respirators free of charge when PM2.5 exceeds 35.4 ug/m3 \(AQI > 100\).) Tj T*
(3. Work-Rest Cycles: Implement mandatory 15-minute indoor rest breaks per hour in air-conditioned break areas when AQI exceeds 150.) Tj T*
(4. Workload Adjustment: Shift heavy manual labor tasks to early morning hours when ozone and PM levels are lowest.) Tj T*
ET
